From 57f9c3f68df4fd86200e37dca30989334650597e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:19:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 79/82] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon_mem_free keeps the wrapper
 only when the destroy did nothing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 3 item 2 (nvkmd_horizon memory objects)
Why: nvkmd_horizon_mem_free returned without freeing the nvkmd wrapper
 on every failure of horizon_gpu_mem_destroy. That is right for
 ERR_BUSY, which memory.h defines as "nothing happened: the object is
 intact and still owned by the caller", and wrong for every other
 status, which the same contract defines as "the destroy completed and
 the error describes what it cost" — ERR_NV in particular means the
 backing pages were deliberately leaked rather than returned to the
 heap uncached, and the horizon_gpu object is gone. Keeping the wrapper
 then keeps a dangling gpu_mem pointer alive in an object that nothing
 will free and nothing may use.
Evidence: horizon/include/horizon_gpu/memory.h, on
 horizon_gpu_mem_destroy:
   HORIZON_GPU_ERR_NV — the object is GONE and must NOT be passed here
     again; a second call is a use-after-free ...
   BUSY is therefore the only retryable one. Everything else means the
   destroy completed, and the error describes what it cost.
 nvkmd_horizon_mem.c: `if (res.status != HORIZON_GPU_OK) { mesa_loge(...);
 return; }` ahead of FREE(mem).
 Class X: cross-built; the ERR_NV path needs svcSetMemoryAttribute to
 refuse a restore, which no console run has produced.
Upstream: no — the backend is Horizon's.
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c
index b30db0c..4aa105d 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c
@@ -36,7 +36,15 @@ nvkmd_horizon_mem_free(struct nvkmd_mem *_mem)
        */
       mesa_loge("horizon_gpu_mem_destroy failed: status %d, nv 0x%08" PRIx32,
                 (int)res.status, res.nv);
-      return;
+      /* BUSY is the one answer that means "nothing happened": the
+       * object is intact and the wrapper still owns it, so both stay.
+       * Every other failure means the destroy COMPLETED and the error
+       * says what it cost (memory.h: ERR_NV is a backing deliberately
+       * leaked rather than returned uncached to the heap). The
+       * horizon_gpu object is gone then, and a wrapper kept around it
+       * would be a dangling pointer nobody may pass anywhere again. */
+      if (res.status == HORIZON_GPU_ERR_BUSY)
+         return;
    }
 
    FREE(mem);
